  "id": "phoenix",
  "intro": "Phoenix is a rare combination: a very large metro with almost no terrain and almost no rain, which is as good as VHF propagation gets in a city. It is also ringed by military aviation — Luke to the west runs fighter training all week, and there is more military AM traffic in 225–380 MHz here than almost anywhere outside Nevada. The flying season is the opposite of everywhere else: the sky is busiest between November and April, and in July the heat is genuinely a flight-planning problem you will hear discussed on the air.",
  "introz": "凤凰城是个少见的组合：一个几乎没有地形起伏、也几乎不下雨的超大都会区，这对城市里的 VHF 传播来说已是极限。它还被军事航空环绕——西面的卢克空军基地整周都在进行战斗机训练，225–380 MHz 的军航 AM 通话量仅次于内华达。这里的飞行季节和别处相反：十一月到次年四月天空最忙，而七月的高温是真正会在频道里被讨论的飞行计划问题。",
